<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">The Audited consolidated financial results for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2020 have been reviwed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting  nheld on November 27, 2020. The Statutory Auditors have expressed an unmodified review opinion. These consolidated financial results are prepared in accourdance with the Indian Accounting  nStandards (Ind AS) as prescribed under Section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013, read with Rule 3 of the Companies (Indian Acconting Standrads) Rule, 2015 and Companies (Indian Accounting  nStandards) Amendment Rules, 2016.  nThe Group operates only in 'construction, development and sale of real estate' segment and operates only in India accordingly segment related information is as reflected in the financial results.  nPrevious period figures have been regrouped / rearranged and re-classified wherever necessary to confirm to current period's classification.  nImpact of Covid 19 :-  nThe World Health Organisation (WHO) declared outbreak of Coronavirus Disease (COVID-19) a global pandemic on March 11, 2020. Consequent to this, Government of India declared lockdown on  nMarch 23, 2020 and the Group suspended the operations in all ongoing projects of the Group in compliance with the lockdown instructions issued by the Central and State Governments. COVID-19  nhas impacted the normal business operations of the Group like others during the lock-down period.  nThe Group has assessed the possible effects that may result from the pandemic relating to COVID-19 on the carrying amounts of Receivables, Inventories, Investments and other assets / liabilities. In  ndeveloping the assumptions relating to the possible future uncertainties in the global economic conditions because of this pandemic, the Group, as at the date of approval of these financial results has  nused internal and external sources of Information. As on current date, the Group has concluded that the Impact of COVID - 19 is not material based on these estimates.  nThe Central and State Governments have initiated steps to lift the lockdown and the Group will adhere to the same as it resumes its activities, the Group will continue to monitor developments in  nfuture periods.  nDuring the period April to September 2020 due to Covid 19 lockdown the Group has paid sustainability advance to its employees. The Group will process the payroll once the situation returns to  nnormalcy and also discharge its liabilities. TDS is not due on the sustainability advance paid to employees and other statutory liabilities like provident fund, professional tax, ESIC, etc., for the period  nupto September 2020 on the sustainability advance has been deposited alongwith interest subsequent to period end.  nAs on today the outstanding statutory liabilities for the period upto Septemeber 2020 after adjusting the payment made subsequent to period end is as under:payment made subsequent to period end is as under:</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
